    {
      "title": "Eisenkot targets Netanyahu-era policies as new Israeli parliament convenes",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/eisenkot-targets-netanyahu-era-policies-as-new-israeli-parliament-convenes-126111001083_1.html",
      "description": "Gadi Eisenkot, the politician tasked with forming a new Israeli government, pledged on Tuesday to reverse many of Benjamin Netanyahu's policies as the new parliament was sworn in.\nThe pledge sets the stage for a consequential month of legislative action and coalition negotiations. Eisenkot, a former military chief, has up to six weeks to form a government that would end the tenure of Israel's longest-serving prime minister.\nWhile it remains unclear whether Eisenkot will be able to forge a coalition government, the new Knesset can enact legislation in the meantime. Netanyahu's opponents now control a solid majority in parliament.\nEisenkot's bloc introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into Hamas' October 7, 2023, attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the power",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-11T02:21:36"
    }
